  "reason": "Evidence: config_020 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat) achieved the best accuracy (0.507) and is also cheaper (3.95 GPU hrs) than config_006 (resnet50 variant, 0.471, 9.06 GPU hrs), confirming that the ViT-L image encoder and scgpt RNA encoder with transformer aggregation are a strong combination. Uncertainty: we have only tested concat fusion so far; weighted fusion could better balance the two modalities' contributions, especially if one modality dominates. This experiment (config_019) changes only the fusion mechanism from concat to weighted while keeping the best-performing scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer stack, providing a clean single-variable comparison to determine whether learned fusion weights improve over simple concatenation. It is the best next step because it directly exploits the strongest evidence with minimal additional risk, is likely to cost ~4 GPU hours (same architecture as config_020), and with 7 experiments remaining, confirming or refuting the fusion hypothesis early will guide whether to further explore aggregation/encoder variations or pivot to unimodal baselines."
